@startuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #FFE5CC
skinparam boxBackgroundColor #F0F0F0

title SafeCore - Security Audit Flow (Complete Sequence Diagram)

actor "Authenticated\nUser" as User
participant "DashboardController\n<<UI>>" as Dashboard
participant "SecurityAuditService\n<<Business>>" as AuditService
participant "VaultService\n<<Business>>" as VaultService
participant "PasswordStrengthEvaluator\n<<Security>>" as StrengthEval
participant "EncryptionStrategy\n<<Security>>" as Encryption
participant "PasswordEntryRepository\n<<Persistence>>" as Repository
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Security Audit Initiation ==

User -> Dashboard: Clicks "Security Audit" button
activate Dashboard

Dashboard -> Dashboard: Show audit overlay

Dashboard -> AuditService: runAudit()
activate AuditService

note right of AuditService
  Audit analyzes vault for:
  - Weak passwords (< STRONG)
  - Old passwords (> 1 year)
  - Reused passwords (duplicates)
end note

== Retrieve All Vault Entries ==

AuditService -> VaultService: getEntriesForCurrentUser()
activate VaultService

VaultService -> VaultService: SessionContext.getCurrentUserEmail()
VaultService -> Repository: findByUserEmail(email)
activate Repository
Repository -> DB: SELECT * FROM password_entries\nWHERE user_email = ?\nORDER BY created_at DESC
DB --> Repository: List<PasswordEntryEntity>
Repository --> VaultService: List<PasswordEntryEntity>
deactivate Repository

VaultService --> AuditService: List<PasswordEntryEntity>
deactivate VaultService

alt Vault is empty
    AuditService -> AuditService: Create perfect audit:\nscore=100, weak=0, old=0, reused=0
    AuditService --> Dashboard: AuditResult(100, 0, 0, 0, 0)
    Dashboard --> User: "Perfect! No entries to audit"
    deactivate AuditService
    deactivate Dashboard
else Vault has entries

    == Decrypt All Passwords for Analysis ==

    loop For each PasswordEntryEntity
        AuditService -> VaultService: decryptPassword(entry.encryptedPassword)
        activate VaultService

        VaultService -> Encryption: decrypt(encryptedBytes)
        activate Encryption

        Encryption -> Encryption: Extract IV (first 16 bytes)
        Encryption -> Encryption: Extract ciphertext (remaining bytes)
        Encryption -> Encryption: Initialize AES cipher (DECRYPT mode)\nKey: 256-bit\nIV: extracted\nMode: CBC\nPadding: PKCS5
        Encryption -> Encryption: cipher.doFinal(ciphertext)

        Encryption --> VaultService: plainPassword (String)
        deactivate Encryption

        VaultService --> AuditService: plainPassword
        deactivate VaultService
    end

    note right of AuditService
      Now we have:
      - All entries (metadata)
      - All decrypted passwords (plaintext)
      Ready for analysis
    end note

    == Analyze Weak Passwords ==

    loop For each decrypted password
        AuditService -> StrengthEval: evaluate(password)
        activate StrengthEval

        StrengthEval -> StrengthEval: Check length >= 8
        StrengthEval -> StrengthEval: Count criteria:\n- lowercase\n- uppercase\n- digits\n- symbols
        StrengthEval -> StrengthEval: Calculate score

        alt Score < 4 criteria OR length < 8
            StrengthEval --> AuditService: Strength.WEAK
            AuditService -> AuditService: weakCount++
            AuditService -> AuditService: Add to weakServices list
        else Score == 3 criteria
            StrengthEval --> AuditService: Strength.MEDIUM
            AuditService -> AuditService: weakCount++ (not STRONG)
            AuditService -> AuditService: Add to weakServices list
        else Score == 4 criteria
            StrengthEval --> AuditService: Strength.STRONG
            AuditService -> AuditService: (no penalty)
        end
        deactivate StrengthEval
    end

    == Analyze Old Passwords ==

    loop For each entry
        AuditService -> AuditService: Check if createdAt < (now - 1 year)
        alt Password older than 1 year
            AuditService -> AuditService: oldCount++
        end
    end

    == Analyze Reused Passwords ==

    AuditService -> AuditService: Group passwords by value
    AuditService -> AuditService: Find duplicates

    loop For each duplicate group
        AuditService -> AuditService: reusedCount += (group.size - 1)
        note right
          If same password used 3 times,
          we count 2 reuses
        end note
    end

    == Calculate Health Score ==

    AuditService -> AuditService: Calculate score:\nbase = 100\nscore -= (weakCount × 10)\nscore -= (oldCount × 5)\nscore -= (reusedCount × 15)

    note right of AuditService
      Scoring penalties:
      - Weak password: -10 points
      - Old password: -5 points
      - Reused password: -15 points

      Final score = max(0, calculated_score)
    end note

    AuditService -> AuditService: Create AuditResult:\n- score\n- weakCount\n- oldCount\n- reusedCount\n- totalPasswords

    AuditService --> Dashboard: AuditResult
    deactivate AuditService

    == Display Results to User ==

    Dashboard -> Dashboard: Update UI with results

    Dashboard -> Dashboard: Set health score label

    alt Score >= 80
        Dashboard -> Dashboard: Set indicator GREEN
        Dashboard -> Dashboard: Message: "Excellent security!"
    else Score >= 50
        Dashboard -> Dashboard: Set indicator YELLOW
        Dashboard -> Dashboard: Message: "Good, but can improve"
    else Score < 50
        Dashboard -> Dashboard: Set indicator RED
        Dashboard -> Dashboard: Message: "Security needs attention!"
    end

    Dashboard -> Dashboard: Display weak passwords count
    Dashboard -> Dashboard: Display old passwords count
    Dashboard -> Dashboard: Display reused passwords count

    Dashboard -> Dashboard: Generate recommendations:\n"- Strengthen weak passwords\n- Update old passwords\n- Use unique passwords"

    Dashboard --> User: Show audit results overlay
    deactivate Dashboard

    == User Actions Post-Audit ==

    alt User wants to improve
        User -> Dashboard: Identifies weak/old/reused entries
        User -> Dashboard: Updates passwords one by one
        note right
          User can:
          - Edit weak entries
          - Generate new strong passwords
          - Delete old unused entries
          - Run audit again to verify
        end note
    else User closes audit
        User -> Dashboard: Clicks "Close"
        Dashboard -> Dashboard: Hide audit overlay
    end
end

== Post-Audit State ==

note over User, DB
  Audit complete with:
  - Health score calculated
  - Vulnerabilities identified
  - Recommendations provided
  - No data modified (read-only analysis)
  - User aware of security posture
end note

@enduml

